-- --- mission 4, Scrap Truce: E phrygian dominant, the fast one, and the only piece that changes key: bars 9 to 14 are a real move to D harmonic minor, pivoted in by an A7 and returned by a Bb-F-E cadence. The hook puts its long note on the augmented second and leaves two rests, so it has a silhouette.
-- 76 bars, 3m02s. Movements (in bars): I 8, II 10, III 6, IV 12, V 12, VI 12, VII 16.
-- The lead runs from level 58 to 100 across them. Movement I is the piece as
-- it was written; everything after it develops that material. ---

